{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault","id":1279026,"title":"Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation on the Storytellers Vault","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-06T12:47:30-08:00","id":1279026,"title":"Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation on the Storytellers Vault","content":"For those that don't follow the Vault thread in the main Chronicles of Darkness forum, I figured I'd post this here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/263371.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\"> Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation - 2/17/2019: Updated with quick casting/purchasing reference. Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation takes the systems presen </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation </b>takes the systems presented in <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</a>, and updates them for 2<sup>nd</sup> edition, expanding upon the improvised ritual systems provided in every way. There\u2019s more Themes, more rituals, more options, and more systems defined for it, and of course, more Risk to enacting these dark magics. It includes:<ul><li>A complete redevelopment of Blood Sorcery, providing them with a \u201csingle roll\u201d ritual system that allows for improvised rituals, studied rites, and mastered miracles, providing more options than ever before.</li> <li>New and updated rituals and Merits, including a simplified system for Threnodies; magic that any Kindred can tap into by ritualizing their Disciplines.</li> <li>Three unique forms of Blood Sorcery used by cults, bloodlines, or those seeking power from whatever source they can find.&quot;</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In essence, it's a 2e update of Sacraments and Blasphemies, allowing for more options while removing a few issues the old system had or didn't account for. And yes, it takes some cues from Mage 2e instead of Mage 1e.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T18:48:54-08:00","id":1279094,"title":"","content":"Having not looked at it yet, would you comment on how portable it might be to an effort for representing a proper VtR-ing of Tremere blood sorcery paths?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:10:29-08:00","id":1279098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1279094#post1279094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having not looked at it yet, would you comment on how portable it might be to an effort for representing a proper VtR-ing of Tremere blood sorcery paths?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's both good and bad for it. Good because it can easily provide mechanics for nearly all of the Tremere paths (minus a few exceptions based on the limits of Blood Sorcery). Bad because it's a more open ended system, rather than providing specific Paths to go off of like owod Blood Sorcery. It brings a touch of Mage's open-endedness to rituals, although keeps them lengthy, visceral, and (usually) anchored within physical reality.<br /> <br /> But you could, say, use this system to create &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; as the Ritual Discipline, with some hermetic style Motifs (the thematics a Ritual Discipline has to follow for its effects, and the mechanical advantage you get for doing so) and then have Paths be represented by groupings of Mastered rituals (rituals that are cast in the span of a half minute or so instead of a half hour, but cost a fair bit of XP for each), perhaps something that's granted more easily to them as part of how their magic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:22:06-08:00","id":1279243,"title":"","content":"Really glad wanted a Safer version of pool of forbidden truths a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T18:26:43-08:00","id":1279361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1279098#post1279098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's both good and bad for it. Good because it can easily provide mechanics for nearly all of the Tremere paths (minus a few exceptions based on the limits of Blood Sorcery). Bad because it's a more open ended system, rather than providing specific Paths to go off of like owod Blood Sorcery. It brings a touch of Mage's open-endedness to rituals, although keeps them lengthy, visceral, and (usually) anchored within physical reality.<br /> <br /> But you could, say, use this system to create &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; as the Ritual Discipline, with some hermetic style Motifs (the thematics a Ritual Discipline has to follow for its effects, and the mechanical advantage you get for doing so) and then have Paths be represented by groupings of Mastered rituals (rituals that are cast in the span of a half minute or so instead of a half hour, but cost a fair bit of XP for each), perhaps something that's granted more easily to them as part of how their magic works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So... might I characterize it as a set of building blocks from which one could successfully define a set of path &quot;rituals&quot; to accomplish desired game effects? Your comment about treating path results as mini-rituals is actually very interesting.<br /> <br /> This is all just a point that I've been pondering for years, and haven't really seen a 2e solution to yet. So: intriguing. (And yes, a direct port of <i>all</i> WoD paths is an exceptionally unwise thing to do as they would flat-out break the setting rules. Lure of Flames for example.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T20:01:44-08:00","id":1279379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1279361#post1279361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So... might I characterize it as a set of building blocks from which one could successfully define a set of path &quot;rituals&quot; to accomplish desired game effects? Your comment about treating path results as mini-rituals is actually very interesting.<br /> <br /> This is all just a point that I've been pondering for years, and haven't really seen a 2e solution to yet. So: intriguing. (And yes, a direct port of <i>all</i> WoD paths is an exceptionally unwise thing to do as they would flat-out break the setting rules. Lure of Flames for example.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you could easily use the systems for something like that. To oversimplify it, if your rating's high enough, you can do anything your &quot;Themes&quot; say you can do, which is fairly wide and varied, so long as they fit the thematics for the Discipline, and then you can also buy rituals individually as learned (higher dice pool, safer casting) or Mastered (quicker casting time, measured in a few turns by default).<br /> <br /> And yeah, stuff like Lure of Flames is mostly out of reach. Minus some very very specific exceptions documented in the book....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T05:59:47-08:00","id":1279453,"title":"","content":"So any reviews for this yet? I personally don't fancy the idea of dropping 15$ for what is essentially a book of homebrew without knowing how good the quality is or how much it changes from first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:02:17-08:00","id":1279506,"title":"","content":"its an ok book... Though I think it could use a few more Threnodys...<br /> <br /> And not sure what a 'Step' is is it just additional succeses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:02:23-08:00","id":1279527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1279453#post1279453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So any reviews for this yet? I personally don't fancy the idea of dropping 15$ for what is essentially a book of homebrew without knowing how good the quality is or how much it changes from first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a review on the Vault page and some ratings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1279506#post1279506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its an ok book... Though I think it could use a few more Threnodys...<br /> <br /> And not sure what a 'Step' is is it just additional succeses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Threnodies weren't meant to be a main focus of the book, but it's not too hard to make more for them. Maybe I can work up a free little add on with a few more of them.<br /> <br /> As for steps: &quot;For each dot in the primary Theme of the ritual above the first, and for each additional -2 penalty taken in the casting dice pool, one step above the basic success can be applied to one of the factors below&quot;<br /> It's just the term used for increasing ritual factors, gained with penalties or by having a high Theme rating. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:56:55-08:00","id":1279545,"title":"","content":"Ok to make Stolen Vitae last a week, I'd have to add 1 extra step.<br /> <br /> That means -2 to my penalty?<br /> But it also means I wont have to use the ritual again for a whole nother week.<br /> <br /> <br /> making it last a month is bad.... as few kindred could survive that long without taking in new Vitae...<br /> <br /> <br /> But if Im a BP 6+ Member of the circle I need to feed somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T19:09:48-07:00","id":1302418,"title":"","content":"For anyone that's gotten this, and likes to do strange bits of crossover like me, I've added a post on my Patreon with Fae Sorcery, which is Blood Sorcery using <b>Rites of Damnation</b>'s systems along with some <b>Changeling</b> 2e crossover bits (like Goblin Debt).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/fae-sorcery-25860322\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/fae-sorcery-25860322</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T21:43:11-07:00","id":1310475,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">oh still curious on one thing? on this PDF</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the improved versions of Apple of Eden and pool of forbidden truths whats it like does it shield the mind from what its experiencing? </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T22:14:05-07:00","id":1310480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1310475#post1310475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">oh still curious on one thing? on this PDF</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the improved versions of Apple of Eden and pool of forbidden truths whats it like does it shield the mind from what its experiencing? </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, the way it works is if you use the &quot;Motif&quot; to learn it as a lower level ritual, the effect on either is similar to in SotC; Forbidden Truths gives you the condition, and apple of eden causes a breaking point. If you improvise it or Learn it as the normal level without the motif, it's not relying on Cruac corrupting you or the holy nature of apple of eden burning through you with its power, so you can consider them comparatively &quot;gentle&quot; versions of the rituals. It's still likely unsettling, but not so much of a mind break as to cause the related condition/breaking point. Case of the scalpel vs the hatchet sort of methodology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T09:57:58-07:00","id":1317201,"title":"","content":"one more Thing I'd like to ask on &quot;Stole vitae&quot; How difficult do you think it would be to make a 3rd party the beneficiary?<br /> <br /> Think it would work? <br /> <br /> Seems to me like something They'd want to be able to do to grant a boon to Elders who are willing to indebt themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T16:38:15-07:00","id":1317247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1317201#post1317201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one more Thing I'd like to ask on &quot;Stole vitae&quot; How difficult do you think it would be to make a 3rd party the beneficiary?<br /> <br /> Think it would work?<br /> <br /> Seems to me like something They'd want to be able to do to grant a boon to Elders who are willing to indebt themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think taht would work fine, sure. I'd add another to the required Scale, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T22:28:20-07:00","id":1339765,"title":"","content":"Question on anyone familiar with the Blood Sorceries: Rites of Damnation.<br /> <br /> I am trying to make sure I understand a complete casting example.<br /> If someone could give me a casting example for Vitae Reliquary, storing 5 Vitae, and lasting for 1 month that would be great.<br /> <br /> Part of what is tripping me up is the following bolded section<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The following factors define various aspects of a ritual\u2019s reach and effect, measured in \u201csteps.\u201d <b>For each dot in the primary Theme of the ritual above the first</b>, and for each additional -2 penalty taken in the casting dice pool, one step above the basic success can be applied to one of the factors below. </div> </div> </div>As in Mage 2E, I understand that as I bump up the steps I take -2d penalty to the dice pool.<br /> I understand that for each Basic Factor I switch to Advanced I add 2d of Risk.<br /> The bolded line almost sounds like Free Steps, and if so would it be Theme dots -1, Theme dots - Ritual Level<br /> <br /> Also do I only need one success to make this happen, a 2E standard, or is there a number of success equal to ritual level or anything.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachme