Relight","date":". 10-17-2023, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T19:53:41-07:00","id":1533439,"title":"","content":"Hello \ud83d\udc4b\ud83c\udffb, sorry for thread Necro, but I have a question about motif, and thought this would be a good place to ask.<br /> <br /> Basically, I have some questions about motifs,<br /> <br /> - How do I define if a discipline should be able to do an improvised rite? For instance for Cattiveria would be simple, because need to be something death related, but Cruac and Theban Sorcery seems much more open ended, maybe an example of something that each discipline should be able to achieve and the other no, could be helpful for me.<br /> - What would be good implementations of a motif in a rite? In the narrative sense, the book mention that should always implement motif, but not sure how deep should it be, spilling blood should be enough for cruac or should be something deeper? Maybe some examples of what would be valid could help me.<br /> - What kind of bonuses should a motif be able to give for a rite? Like the options some rites give for additional effect.<br /> <br /> sorry, for any typo, is really late where I live haha<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T22:52:02-07:00","id":1534015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1533439#post1533439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello \ud83d\udc4b\ud83c\udffb, sorry for thread Necro, but I have a question about motif, and thought this would be a good place to ask.<br /> <br /> Basically, I have some questions about motifs,<br /> <br /> - How do I define if a discipline should be able to do an improvised rite? For instance for Cattiveria would be simple, because need to be something death related, but Cruac and Theban Sorcery seems much more open ended, maybe an example of something that each discipline should be able to achieve and the other no, could be helpful for me.<br /> - What would be good implementations of a motif in a rite? In the narrative sense, the book mention that should always implement motif, but not sure how deep should it be, spilling blood should be enough for cruac or should be something deeper? Maybe some examples of what would be valid could help me.<br /> - What kind of bonuses should a motif be able to give for a rite? Like the options some rites give for additional effect.<br /> <br /> sorry, for any typo, is really late where I live haha<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>-Well, this can be complicated as those two are <b>purposely</b> pretty open ended as they're the major covenant advantages. Still, something like how Theban Sorcery can create an &quot;angel&quot; probably can't possibly be reproduced by Cruac, and in turn Cruac's ability to become a spirit of an area likely can't be mirrored by Theban.<br /> -For the sake of the narrative component, it's just meant to guide how the rituals should &quot;look&quot; when you cast them. Cruac will involve blood rites, sacrifices, orgiastic celebrations, and idols, whereas Theban is more focused, calm, and holy in nature. A Theban Rite is more likely to be fluffed as condemning someone whereas Cruac will word it like a bestial curse.<br /> - Mechanically, the most common and obvious one is obviously being able to Learn the rite with fewer Themes (usually just one, after my most recent update). But for Level one rites, and others where you can't see letting it just be cast at a lower level, work in reverse. Maybe the level one rite has some level-two adjacent benefits, or it adds on a component you normally need another theme for (especially Divination 2's triggers and Guidance 2's selective effects). Similarly, maybe it does something you'd normally need Risk for, without the Risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T15:47:22-07:00","id":1534058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534015#post1534015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Well, this can be complicated as those two are <b>purposely</b> pretty open ended as they're the major covenant advantages. Still, something like how Theban Sorcery can create an &quot;angel&quot; probably can't possibly be reproduced by Cruac, and in turn Cruac's ability to become a spirit of an area likely can't be mirrored by Theban.<br /> -For the sake of the narrative component, it's just meant to guide how the rituals should &quot;look&quot; when you cast them. Cruac will involve blood rites, sacrifices, orgiastic celebrations, and idols, whereas Theban is more focused, calm, and holy in nature. A Theban Rite is more likely to be fluffed as condemning someone whereas Cruac will word it like a bestial curse.<br /> - Mechanically, the most common and obvious one is obviously being able to Learn the rite with fewer Themes (usually just one, after my most recent update). But for Level one rites, and others where you can't see letting it just be cast at a lower level, work in reverse. Maybe the level one rite has some level-two adjacent benefits, or it adds on a component you normally need another theme for (especially Divination 2's triggers and Guidance 2's selective effects). Similarly, maybe it does something you'd normally need Risk for, without the Risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for taking some time answering, I can visualize it much better now, thanks \ud83d\ude42.<br /> <br /> Now that you mentioned risk. There's any guideline of how much risk is appropriate for a given improvement?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T13:27:11-07:00","id":1534105,"title":"","content":"My main goal is to have more predefined 2e Blood Sorcery spells available for my players and NPCs. I don\u2019t necessarily need a system to create new spells. At least for now.<br /> <br /> General questions:<br /> 1) What are the differences between 1e and 2e spells? <br /> 2) Are there other books with interesting Blood Sorcery spells that are still usable with 2e, or could be easily updated with the answers provided by question 1?<br /> <br /> Book related questions:<br /> 1) Are all spells from the 1e book included?<br /> 2) Does the 1e book contain content that the 2e book doesn\u2019t?<br /> (I try to better understand the differences of the content besides being 1e and 2e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T13:06:27-07:00","id":1534409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534105#post1534105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main goal is to have more predefined 2e Blood Sorcery spells available for my players and NPCs. I don\u2019t necessarily need a system to create new spells. At least for now.<br /> <br /> General questions:<br /> 1) What are the differences between 1e and 2e spells?<br /> 2) Are there other books with interesting Blood Sorcery spells that are still usable with 2e, or could be easily updated with the answers provided by question 1?<br /> <br /> Book related questions:<br /> 1) Are all spells from the 1e book included?<br /> 2) Does the 1e book contain content that the 2e book doesn\u2019t?<br /> (I try to better understand the differences of the content besides being 1e and 2e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be wrong in some answers, because was long ago that I read both books completely.<br /> <br /> What you mean by predefined? Just don't have option to create spells? Why not core Blood Sorcery? Or maybe NMD take on it?<br /> <br /> 1) I think the main one is casting time, 1e was basically instant casting, 2nd takes at least 15mins (core) or 2 turns in this supplement.<br /> <br /> 2) This book is a good supplement for it. You could try Bloodlines the Resurrected, or None More Dark Requiem for Rome. I think there's a VtR Errata with the systems too.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAbout the book<br /> 1) not sure, I guess not<br /> 2) yep, a lot. Basically update all the content of the original book for something more akin to 2nd edition mage (1st edition was akin to 1st edition mage). So, lots of new mechanics, merits and etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T21:33:31-07:00","id":1534571,"title":"","content":"I must say that it was nice that the supplement included a power relating to the pre-existent souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T04:31:49-07:00","id":1536150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534409#post1534409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you mean by predefined?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ready to use Blood Magic spells from the books that I did not create myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534409#post1534409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bOr maybe NMD take on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat is NMD?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534409#post1534409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not core Blood Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI assume you mean the few spells from the V:TR 2e book. Because there are not really many of them. I would like to have a larger list of spells/rituals I can choose from for my NPCs and players. My preferred choice would be official material, but most of it is 1e. <br /> <br /> (I would like to create a town in South Britain (Dartmoor) as my focus point where the Circle of the Crone is the largest covenant.) <br /> <br /> So I suppose I should get one of those books or both. I am not sure...<br /> <br /> I also bought the Circle of the Crone book, because I found \u201eSecrets of the Covenants\u201c not so helpful to portray the covenant or to extend my spells. That\u2019s also one of the reason why I asked for Blood Sorcery conversion tipps. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014<br /> <br /> Sometimes I feel like Onyx Path abandoned V:TR 2e somewhere in the middle. At least an official conversion guide would be really nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T13:54:36-07:00","id":1538252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1534058#post1534058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you so much for taking some time answering, I can visualize it much better now, thanks \ud83d\ude42.<br /> <br /> Now that you mentioned risk. There's any guideline of how much risk is appropriate for a given improvement?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's honestly something I just eyeball. +1 is for minor improvements, +2 is for significant ones, +3 for a major benefit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main goal is to have more predefined 2e Blood Sorcery spells available for my players and NPCs. I don\u2019t necessarily need a system to create new spells. At least for now.<br /> <br /> General questions:<br /> 1) What are the differences between 1e and 2e spells?<br /> 2) Are there other books with interesting Blood Sorcery spells that are still usable with 2e, or could be easily updated with the answers provided by question 1?<br /> <br /> Book related questions:<br /> 1) Are all spells from the 1e book included?<br /> 2) Does the 1e book contain content that the 2e book doesn\u2019t?<br /> (I try to better understand the differences of the content besides being 1e and 2e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>1e rituals had predefined success ratings based on ritual level and were cast with a roll per turn. There are some other minor differences but that's the big one.<br /> <br /> Honestly you probably just want to look into Desecrated Rites instead: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331129/Desecrated-Rites?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=259490</a><br /> It uses the basic sorcery system instead of the new one in Rites of Damnation, but has a lot of 1e rituals converted to 2e, and a handful of new ones. Among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:15:50-07:00","id":1539031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1279026-blood-sorcery-rites-of-damnation-on-the-storytellers-vault?p=1536150#post1536150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ready to use Blood Magic spells from the books that I did not create myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What is NMD?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI assume you mean the few spells from the V:TR 2e book. Because there are not really many of them. I would like to have a larger list of spells/rituals I can choose from for my NPCs and players. My preferred choice would be official material, but most of it is 1e.<br /> <br /> (I would like to create a town in South Britain (Dartmoor) as my focus point where the Circle of the Crone is the largest covenant.)<br /> <br /> So I suppose I should get one of those books or both. I am not sure...<br /> <br /> I also bought the Circle of the Crone book, because I found \u201eSecrets of the Covenants\u201c not so helpful to portray the covenant or to extend my spells. That\u2019s also one of the reason why I asked for Blood Sorcery conversion tipps. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014<br /> <br /> Sometimes I feel like Onyx Path abandoned V:TR 2e somewhere in the middle. At least an official conversion guide would be really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply.<br /> <br /> By NMD I mean No More Dark, they are a third party publishers with professional level quality, I think several writers of them used to write for Onyx Path itself.<br /> <br /> By core sorcery, I mean the rules from the core book, that is, the spell from corebook but, from Secrets of Covenants too, and Thousands Years, or all third party based on the core rules, using extended action, of 15 minutes interval (if I am not mistaken) and such. <br /> <br /> I would recommend for you to take a look at Bloodlines: the Resurrected, it may give you more spells too. And Requiem for Rome from NMD, could give you some help. If you are willing to invest a bit more time, Rites of Damnation from Falco has ready made rituals too, but you still need to figure out the factor when casting it.<br /> <br /> I completely agree, everytime I start a new game that will have vampires, I burn a bit of my brain to decide which system to use, and almost never is the core one. It's kinda sad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:17:11-07:00","id":1539032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by 